{"content_hash": "sha256:cb0de2f7f017396890f7eb45d86416c2df0946101be8adfb347b82b6f9c8d065", "evidence_kind": "COUNTEREXAMPLE", "id": "evidence:2602.18939v1:fixed-window-monotonicity-counterexample", "legacy_record_id": "statement:2602.18939v1:fixed-window-monotonicity-claimed", "produced_at": "2026-08-22T00:00:00Z", "provenance": {"checked_values": {"final": "sqrt(2)", "initial": "1", "operation": "R_X(pi/2) Clifford"}, "claimir_truth_status_mutation": false, "downstream_policy": "EXCLUDE_AS_THEOREM_DEPENDENCY", "proposition_ref": "math-proposition-ir:2602.18939v1:fixed-window-counterexample@1", "review_path": "agents/predicting-magic-from-very-few-measurements/reviews/reduced-rom-monotonicity-counterexample.md", "source_claim_classification": "REFUTED", "target_math_claim_ir": "math-claim-ir:2602.18939v1:fixed-window-monotonicity-claimed", "verification_record": "verification:2602.18939v1:fixed-window-monotonicity-audit"}, "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.migration-evidence/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:2602.18939v1:fixed-window-monotonicity-claim", "anchor:2602.18939v1:fixed-window-monotonicity-proof"], "statement": "An exact one-qubit calculation with the fixed window {X,Z} gives reduced RoM 1 before and sqrt(2) after the free Clifford rotation exp(-i pi X/4); therefore the source's fixed-window monotonicity assertion is false."}
{"content_hash": "sha256:162a1861bb5a8f9dacf45d9a2d22fb2353aa7a3d5eefa10774d7859c4d303909", "evidence_kind": "SOURCE_AUDIT", "id": "evidence:2602.18939v1:vrep-published-proof-gap", "legacy_record_id": "statement:2602.18939v1:reduced-polytope-vrep", "produced_at": "2026-08-22T00:00:00Z", "provenance": {"claimir_truth_status_mutation": false, "counterexample": "For n=2, M={Z_1,X_2}, and |00>, the measured stabilizer support {Z_1} is not maximal; projection (1,0) is the midpoint of (1,1) and (1,-1).", "review_path": "agents/predicting-magic-from-very-few-measurements/reviews/vrep-proof-gap.md", "verification_record": "verification:2602.18939v1:vrep-proof-audit"}, "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.migration-evidence/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:2602.18939v1:vrep-theorem", "anchor:2602.18939v1:vrep-proof"], "statement": "The published proof does not establish the asserted V-representation: at lines 716-720 it incorrectly infers that a full-rank stabilizer group's signed intersection with the measurement window is maximal, and lines 728-732 do not repair the extremality argument."}
{"content_hash": "sha256:7f2aec5194156066d50bf920ac2dfda6c8cbba98183826c43a4b7cdd8ba22870", "evidence_kind": "COUNTEREXAMPLE", "id": "evidence:2602.18939v1:vrep-literal-coordinate-counterexample", "legacy_record_id": "statement:2602.18939v1:reduced-polytope-vrep", "produced_at": "2026-08-23T00:00:00Z", "provenance": {"claimir_truth_status_mutation": false, "corrected_coordinate_clause": "P in S", "downstream_policy": "EXCLUDE_AS_THEOREM_DEPENDENCY", "measurement_window": "{Z}", "method": "exact one-qubit substitution", "source_claim_classification": "REFUTED", "source_coordinate_clause": "f(P)P in S", "target_math_claim_ir": "math-claim-ir:2602.18939v1:reduced-polytope-vrep"}, "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.migration-evidence/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:2602.18939v1:vrep-theorem", "anchor:2602.18939v1:vrep-proof"], "statement": "For the source theorem read literally, M={Z} and S={Z} give candidate coordinates 1 for f(Z)=+1 and 0 for f(Z)=-1 because the source tests f(Z)Z in S. The asserted convex hull is [0,1], while the projected one-qubit stabilizer polytope is [-1,1]. Thus the literal source V-representation is false; replacing f(P)P in S by P in S belongs only to the external normalized repair."}
